document-2", "question": "What project knowledge is available about \ud83d\udcd6 Informer-Learn \ud83d\udca9\u5c71\u4ee3\u7801 \u00b7 \ud83e\uddea \u5b9e\u9a8c\u5feb\u7167\uff08\u9009\u62e96\u8f6e+\u65e9\u505c\uff09?", "reference": "# \ud83d\udcd6 Informer-Learn \ud83d\udca9\u5c71\u4ee3\u7801\n## \ud83e\uddea \u5b9e\u9a8c\u5feb\u7167\uff08\u9009\u62e96\u8f6e+\u65e9\u505c\uff09\n\n| \u8f6e\u6b21 | R\u00b2 (\u8bad\u7ec3) | R\u00b2 (\u6d4b\u8bd5) | \u5907\u6ce8                         |\n| ---- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------------------------- |\n| 6    | 0.80       | 0.77       | \u65e9\u505c\u5077\u61d2                     |\n| 30   | 0.81       | 0.45       | \u4e0d\u65e9\u505c\u5377\u5230\u5e95\uff08\u6700\u4e0d\u884c\u7684\u4e00\u6b21\uff09 |\n\n> \u6570\u636e\uff1aETTh1 \u7535\u529b\u53d8\u538b\u5668\u5c0f\u65f6\u7ea7\u8bb0\u5f55\n> \u6a21\u578b\uff1a\u5b98\u65b9 Informer \u65e0\u9609\u5272\n> \u6307\u6807\uff1a\u65e0\u8111 R\u00b2 + \u53ef\u89c6\u5316\n>\n> \u4ee3\u7801\uff1a\u6211\u4ee3\u7801\u662f30\u8f6e+\u4e0d\u65e9\u505c\n\n---", "expected_source_ids": ["c76ed657-1572-418d-b44e-56495b1219c1", "f7c069ae-e455-57c9-b40c-2db8856f8ed1"], "source_file": null, "kind": "positive", "must_include": [], "must_not_include": [], "answer_regex": null, "required_tools": [], "expected_tool_calls": [], "response": "## Available project knowledge\n\n**Evidence from the project snapshot**\n- The project is an Informer reproduction using ETTh1 hourly power-transformer data.\n- The snapshot describes the model as the \u201cofficial Informer\u201d without pruning, and lists a sliding-window setup in the repository summary: `seq96 / label48 / pred24`.\n- The reported comparison is:\n  - **6 rounds with early stopping:** training R\u00b2 0.80, test R\u00b2 0.77.\n  - **30 rounds without early stopping:** training R\u00b2 0.81, test R\u00b2 0.45, described as the worst run.\n- The snapshot says the metrics were R\u00b2 and visualizations. The repository summary also describes ProbSparse Attention and a generative decoder.\n\n**What this suggests**\n- In this reported experiment, the 6-round early-stopping run had substantially better test R\u00b2 than the 30-round run, despite a slightly lower training R\u00b2. This is consistent with the snapshot\u2019s claim that early stopping helped generalization.\n\n**Uncertainty**\n- These are project-reported results; the available context contains no run logs or independent verification.\n- The snapshot also says \u201cmy code is 30 rounds + no early stopping,\u201d while the repository summary describes a 6-vs-30 comparison. It is unclear whether the snapshot records a separate experiment or contrasts a proposed setting with the reported runs.\n- No R\u00b2 definition, evaluation protocol, random seeds, or visualization details are provided.\n\n**Team context**\n- The configured team list contains ALice, whose listed role is modeling and whose strengths include deep learning. That does not establish that ALice owns this experiment.\n\n**Useful next step:** Check the experiment code and logs to confirm which configuration produced each score and whether the test evaluation was performed consistently.", "route": "direct_answer", "citations": [], "tool_calls": [], "tool_observations": [], "completion": {"status": "completed", "reason": "fallback_answer_ready", "steps": 0, "tool_call_count": 0, "tool_error_count": 0}, "retrieved_contexts": ["[project_doc] \ud83d\udcd6 Informer-Learn \ud83d\udca9\u5c71\u4ee3\u7801 \u00b7 \ud83e\uddea \u5b9e\u9a8c\u5feb\u7167\uff08\u9009\u62e96\u8f6e+\u65e9\u505c\uff09: # \ud83d\udcd6 Informer-Learn \ud83d\udca9\u5c71\u4ee3\u7801 ## \ud83e\uddea \u5b9e\u9a8c\u5feb\u7167\uff08\u9009\u62e96\u8f6e+\u65e9\u505c\uff09 | \u8f6e\u6b21 | R\u00b2 (\u8bad\u7ec3) | R\u00b2 (\u6d4b\u8bd5) | \u5907\u6ce8 | | ---- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------------------------- | | 6 | 0.80 | 0.77 | \u65e9\u505c\u5077\u61d2 | | 30 | 0.81 | 0.45 | \u4e0d\u65e9\u505c\u5377\u5230\u5e95\uff